     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and well above the 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day ceiling in standard labeling. A single 1,700 mg dose is also much higher than the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nCould you check what was intended? A few possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **A different formulation or dose**, such as extended-release at up to 2,000 mg once daily.\n\nTell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy before it's placed."
      }
     ],
